---
description: ReachLab engineering, evidence, and project conventions
alwaysApply: true
---
ReachLab is a standalone robotics education workbench. Do not import or modify the student's separate physical therapy project.
Use dependency-free JavaScript ES modules and accessible HTML/CSS. All simulation and learning must work locally without credentials, cloud APIs, or CDNs.
Angles in the robotics core are radians. Links and obstacles use consistent simulated millimeter units. The app is a simplified planar kinematic model, not a real robot controller.
Exact geometry must validate every planned motion. The learned collision classifier can be wrong; never let it authorize physical movement or replace the geometry oracle.
Run node --test and node scripts/benchmark.mjs after core changes. Update reproducible results, never invent measurements, user impact, awards, or validation.
Keep AI assistance and real student contributions documented separately. Do not claim student-authored development that was done by assistants.
Do not publish entries, create accounts, spend money, or alter unrelated projects as part of implementation.
